This project is original code (MIT licensed, see LICENSE) built as a
consumer of the FreeInk SDK and informed by three other open-source
projects as architectural/API references. No source code from any of the
projects below is copied into this repository — see docs/architecture.md
for exactly what was reused (a library dependency, a wire format, and API
usage patterns) versus written from scratch.

- FreeInk SDK (https://github.com/Free-Ink/freeink-sdk, MIT License) —
  firmware/ is built directly on this SDK as a PlatformIO library
  dependency (EInkDisplay, SDCardManager, PowerManager, InputManager,
  FreeInkUI). Not modified or forked; used as intended, as a dependency.

- CrossPoint Reader (https://github.com/crosspoint-reader/crosspoint-reader) —
  referenced for how to structure a real FreeInk-based application: its
  PersistableStore (atomic JSON-on-SD persistence) and WifiCredentialStore
  patterns are re-implemented from scratch in firmware/src/store/ and
  firmware/src/config/ against the same design, and its HttpDownloader's
  streaming-to-SD approach informed firmware/src/net/SyncClient.cpp's
  design. No CrossPoint source is linked into this firmware.

- paperlesspaper/paperlessprinter (https://github.com/paperlesspaper/paperlessprinter) —
  referenced for its from-scratch IPP/1.1 wire-protocol implementation
  (attribute encoding, Get-Printer-Attributes response shape, chunked HTTP
  body handling) against a plain http.server, which
  pi-server/xteink_print_server/ipp_server.py reimplements independently
  for this project's narrower needs (see docs/architecture.md for what
  differs).

- phrozen/xtx (https://github.com/phrozen/xtx) — the reference for the
  XTC/XTG/XTCH byte-layout specification (docs/xtc-format.md distills the
  subset this project uses). Both this project's Python encoder
  (pi-server/xteink_print_server/xtc_writer.py) and its C++ decoder
  (firmware/src/xtc/XtcFormat.h) are from-scratch implementations against
  that spec — neither links or vendors the xtx Go module.
